Hi Eun-Gyeong,

I’ve updated the instructions for producing GNSS RO based PBLH files from the raw bufr files. You can find the readme here:
/discover/nobackup/mganesha/DSI_PBL/fromWei/output/readme

The main scripts for converting bufr to netcdf is the “*.j” script below, which is to be run with “gnssro_metadata_bending_angle_nosplits.yaml” for creating the meta data netcdf file, and with “gnssro.yaml” for producing the main refractivity netcdf file. The instructions for editing and running the script are in the readme.
/discover/nobackup/mganesha/DSI_PBL/fromWei/run_bufr2ioda_gnssro.j

Following the conversion from bufr to netcdf, the following python script can be used on the netcdf files to produce PBLH files.
/discover/nobackup/mganesha/DSI_PBL/fromWei/scripts/read_gnssro_twopeaks_wsurfelev_qc_compact.py

I’ve only produced one file to test it, and the output is the same as the file produced using the NCL script that I provided to you (attached is a comparison).  Here is the path to the output file:
/discover/nobackup/mganesha/DSI_PBL/fromWei/scripts/output/twopeaks/thresh40_FPsfcelev_qc/python/firstPBLH/gnssro_pbl_obs_2024090300.nc4

